  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/tormach.cps` (the Tormach PathPilot mill post) now ends every program at the top of Z:\n\n```\nM9          (only when coolant ran)\nM5\nG53 G0 Z0   (or the machine's stated safe Z, #495)\nG20/G21     (only when the EndUnits option asks, #596)\nM30\n```\n\nThe `G30` that followed the final retract is gone, and no `G0 A0` is added. The `G30` before each tool change (`G53 G0 Z0`, `G30`, `T.. M6`) is unchanged. The end retract and the tool-change retract are split: `liftZ()` is the `G53 G0 Z` lift both use, and `retract()` (tool change only) adds the G30. The footer comment is rewritten to the new behaviour and cites #1594 and the user's Hub result.\n\n## Evidence (from the issue)\n\nThe user ran four hand-written endings in PathPilot Hub (770MX sim, v2.14.4, 2026-11-13), with the sim's stored G30 low (machine Z -1.5611):\n\n| Ending | Result |\n|---|---|\n| A: `G53 G0 Z0`, `G30` (the old post) | goes up, then G30 drives the tool down below the part top |\n| B: `G30` only | drives the tool down from Z+0.5 to the G30 Z |\n| C: `G53 G0 Z0` only | ends at the top of travel and stays there |\n| D: `G53 G0 Z0`, `G0 A0` | not wanted |\n\nThe user chose C (\"C is the only right one\"). This PR posts C.\n\n## Fix, not breaking\n\nThe posted output changes only in its last lines, and the change corrects wrong behaviour a user hit (P3 bug), so it is `fix(post)`. No project-file field, parameter or command changes. The reasoning is in `docs/decisions/1594-tormach-end-g53.md`.\n\n## Pins\n\nNew `crates/app/tests/tormach_program_end.rs`:\n- `every_tormach_mill_program_ends_z_up_then_m30_with_no_g30`: every shipped Tormach mill machine ends `M5`, `G53 G0 Z0`, `M30`, with nothing after the final G53 but M30. Both tool changes still read `G53 G0 Z0`, `G30`, `T.. M6`.\n- `a_stated_safe_z_ends_at_that_z_with_no_g30`: a Tormach file stating `safe_retract` 2.0 in ends `G53 G0 Z2`, `M30`, with no G30 anywhere.\n- `a_fourth_axis_program_ends_without_returning_a`: a job indexed to A90 on the 770MX + microARC 4 ends with nothing after the final G53 but M30 (no `G0 A`, no G30).\n\nUpdated to the new ending: `tormach_post::a_pathpilot_program_has_no_fence_and_no_o_or_n_words`, `tormach_safe_retract` (three tests: 2 tool-change G30s plus a G30-free end), `tormach_end_units` (the G20/G21 goes between `G53 G0 Z0` and `M30`).\n\n**Mutation checks** (all restored to green afterwards):\n- Put the G30 back at the end (`onClose` calls `retract()` again): `every_tormach_mill_...` and `a_fourth_axis_...` go red. So do `tormach_post::a_pathpilot_program_...`, both `tormach_end_units` G20/G21 tests, and two `tormach_safe_retract` tests. `a_stated_safe_z_...` stays green, which is correct: a machine with a stated non-zero safe Z never got the G30 (its behaviour is unchanged and pinned).\n- Add `G0 A0` after the end lift: all three new pins go red.\n- Drop the tool-change G30 from `retract()`: `every_tormach_mill_...` goes red.\n\n## Goldens\n\n33 Tormach mill NC goldens changed, and every changed line is the same removed `G30` right before `M30` (`git diff upstream/main -- '*.nc'` shows 33 `-G30` lines and no other `+`/`-` lines). The files:\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach/*` (21, including `index_4face_microarc4`), `inch/tormach/*` (2), `synth_tormach.nc`\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/tormach/*` (7), `crates/post/tests/golden/ream/tormach.nc`\n- `docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th/microarc_test_part.nc`\n\nThe kit README's steps 1 and 7 now describe the new end. No snapshot PNGs are touched. The lathe and plasma goldens are unchanged.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 0 failed. The shared golden inputs changed, so the gate ran the full post suites (28 s) and app suites (812 s), 3337 tests passed. That covers `recorded_post_streams`, `posting`, `recorded_streams`, `script_tormach`, `tormach_post`, `tormach_fourth_axis`, `tormach_end_units`, `tormach_safe_retract`, `tormach_program_end`, `microarc_test_part` and the inch NC goldens.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app` on the touched test targets with `-D warnings`: clean.\n- macOS. Branched from upstream/main 7bfb1824 (newest cut tag v0.19.0); the fork's own main is not synced to that tag.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No PathPilot Hub or machine run of a CamCraft-posted program with this ending. The reference is the user's hand-written program C.\n- No Windows run.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n#1596 (P7): `tormach-plasma.cps` and `tormach-lathe.cps` also end with a bare `G30`, and the mill's tool-change `G30` carries the same low-G30 risk. Both were out of this issue's scope, which covered the mill program end.\n\nChangelog: Tormach PathPilot mill programs now end with `G53 G0 Z0` then `M30`. The trailing `G30` is gone, so a low stored G30 position can no longer drive the tool back down at the end of the program.\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFixes #1594\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
